## 1 - Overview
[up](#table-of-contents)
DDScope is structured around three distinct concerns.

**Core** — the framework-agnostic business logic of DDScope. Core depends only on abstract interfaces — never on a concrete framework or service implementation. It is the portable, ownable heart of the application.

**Framework** — the host shell that launches and wires the application. Core is assembled into a framework at build time. Example: CommWise (current). The framework implements `IFramework` — the abstract interface through which Core interacts with its host.

**Service** — an external capability required by Core, abstracted behind an interface. Multiple implementations of a service can exist; one is selected per assembly. Example: Cytoscape as one implementation of `IGraphRenderer`. Core depends on the interface only — the implementation is injected at application init.

This separation makes DDScope portable: the same Core can be assembled with different frameworks and service implementations without modification.

In the future, an App Modular Architecture convention will be created. The present document will then describe only interfaces and modules.

## 2 - Core Modules
[up](#table-of-contents)
Core is decomposed into modules. Each module has a type that determines how it is packaged and loaded by the host framework.

### Fundamental UI Choice

In all assemblies, DDScope's UI is built on native HTML/CSS/JavaScript. There is no framework-specific UI toolkit, no virtual DOM, no component framework. This is a deliberate architectural choice: it keeps Core portable and ensures that any framework capable of hosting a web page can host DDScope.

### Module Types

| Type | Content | Role |
|---|---|---|
| script | JavaScript only | Business logic, data, services — no markup |
| style | CSS only | Visual definition — layout, colors, typography |
| div | HTML + embedded script | UI components — structure, interaction, event wiring |

Frameworks expose an `IFramework` interface that abstracts module registration and loading. Each framework maps these types to its own packaging model. For an HTML page, script maps to a `<script>` tag, style to a `<style>` or `<link>` tag, and div to an HTML fragment injected into the page body.

### Module Inventory

| Module | Type | Layer | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|---|
| DDS_TOOLS | script | Functional | Transversal utilities, levelled logger |
| DDS_COLORS | script | Functional | Color palette constant |
| DDS_ICONS | script | Functional | SVG icon library |
| DDS_STORE | script | Functional | In-memory CRUD + serialization |
| DDS_DURATION | script | Functional | Duration arithmetic and formatting |
| DDS_MODEL | script | Functional | Cascade delete rules |
| DDS_ACTIONS | script | Functional | Action execution engine |
| DDS_TRANSACTIONS | script | Functional | Snapshot-based undo/redo |
| DDS_TX | script | Functional | Transaction label catalogue |
| DDS_TX_HELPER | script | Functional | UI transaction wrapper |
| DDS_JSON | script | Functional | Project import with ID remapping |
| DDS_NODES | script | Helper | Node CRUD facade |
| DDS_PRODUCTS | script | Helper | Product CRUD facade |
| DDS_FLOWS | script | Helper | Flow CRUD facade |
| DDS_SKUS | script | Helper | SKU CRUD facade |
| DDS_BOMS | script | Helper | BOM CRUD facade |
| DDS_DEMANDS | script | Helper | Demand CRUD facade |
| DDS_ANNOTATIONS | script | Helper | Annotation CRUD facade |
| DDS_LANES | script | Helper | Swim-lane CRUD facade |
| DDS_AI_CONTEXT | script | AI | Project state serialization for AI context |
| DDS_AI | script | AI | Prompt assembly, response parsing, calls IAITransport |
| DDS_LAYOUT | script | Presentation | BFS node placement algorithm |
| DDS_MAP | script + div | Presentation | Map state, Cytoscape wiring, calls IGraphRenderer |
| DDS_SWIMLANES | script + div | Presentation | Swim-lane overlay, calls IGraphRenderer |
| DDS_AI_UI | div | AI | AI panel — plan display, confirm/cancel |
| All *_UI modules | div | Presentation | Table views, panels, modals |
| App styles | style | Presentation | Global CSS — layout, theming, component styles |

## 3 - IFramework
[up](#table-of-contents)
The framework interface abstracts how Core modules are registered, loaded, and initialized by the host.

Core does not call framework APIs directly. At boot, the framework wiring injects itself and all selected service implementations into Core.

See `DDScope_Framework_CommWise.md` for the current implementation.
Full interface specification: to be defined.

## 4 - IGraphRenderer
[up](#table-of-contents)
Abstracts supply chain map rendering and user interaction on the canvas.

Modules that call this interface: DDS_MAP, DDS_SWIMLANES.

See `DDScope_Service_GraphRenderer.md` for implementations and API.
Full interface specification: to be defined.

## 5 - IFileStorage
[up](#table-of-contents)
Abstracts project file persistence — load, save, save-as, dirty state.

Modules that call this interface: DDS_STORE (file operations only).

See `DDScope_Service_FileStorage.md` for implementations and API.
Full interface specification: to be defined.

## 6 - IAITransport
[up](#table-of-contents)
Abstracts Claude API call routing — sends a prompt payload, returns a response.

Modules that call this interface: DDS_AI.

See `DDScope_Service_AITransport.md` for implementations and API.
Full interface specification: to be defined.

## 7 - src Layout
[up](#table-of-contents)
The repository source tree reflects the three-concern structure.

```
src/
  core/                  # All Core modules
  services/
    IGraphRenderer/
      interface.js         # IGraphRenderer abstract definition
      implementation-1/    # First implementation
      implementation-2/    # Second implementation
    IFileStorage/
      interface.js
      implementation-1/
    IAITransport/
      interface.js
      implementation-1/
  frameworks/
    IFramework/
      interface.js         # IFramework abstract definition
    framework-1/           # First framework wiring
    framework-2/
```

Each assembly is a build configuration that selects one framework and one implementation per service. Assemblies are defined in DDScope_Assemblies.md.

